WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.936
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.870
We hope you're doing well,
and now, let's get to the news.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.874
It was announced yesterday
that President Biden

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.343
will follow the FDA
recommendation that those

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:14.380
65 and older receive a
coronavirus vaccine booster.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:19.519
Well, he is used to needing
three shots.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.955
During his address to the U.N.
General assembly today,

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.789
President Biden announced
that the U.S.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.926
will make a $10 billion
commitment to end hunger.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.362
Pretty impressive, especially
compared to the previous

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.865
president who spent about
300 bucks.

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:36.102
Brazilian President
Jair Bolsonaro this morning

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:39.039
entered the U.N. General
Assembly hall unvaccinated,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.709
violating both U.N. rules
and New York law.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:47.013
But he got a hero's welcome
on Staten Island.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.615
Canadian Prime Minister
Justin Trudeau won yesterday's

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:52.418
snap election, and in keeping
with Canadian tradition,

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:56.389
he gave a long, heartfelt
victory apology.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:59.259
President Biden yesterday
recognized the tenth anniversary

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:02.228
of the end of the "Don't ask,
Don't tell" military policy.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:06.732
Now, "Don't ask, Don't tell"
refers to Afghanistan.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.834
Former President Trump sent
a letter last week

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.104
to Georgia's Secretary of State
Brad Raffensperger

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:14.407
asking him to consider
decertifying the 2020 election.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.042
Dude, just give up.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:19.746
You know you don't have to be
President to play golf, right?

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.315
According to a new survey,
9 percent of Americans said

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.418
that they drink less than one
cup of water a day.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.019
At least, I think that's
what they said.

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.689
Their voices were very raspy.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.291
Today was national New York day.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.193
Ah, yes, finally,
a day for New Yorkers

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.694
to think they're special.

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:38.264
"Oh, you're from New York.
Uh-huh.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.366
And you say the pizza
is good there?

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.668
Huh."

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.169
Authorities in New York
are searching for a man

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.738
who allegedly rolled a bike
onto the subway tracks

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.107
over the weekend,
which caused an explosion

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:49.742
when it was hit by a train.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.844
Officials condemn
this behavior and said,

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.713
"When you're done
with the Citi bike,

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.082
you're supposed to chuck it
in the Hudson."

